+# Token count at or above which the empty-index-block guard is compiled in.
+#
+# The guard only pays where index rows carry -1 padding, and padding only exists for
+# queries whose causal prefix is shorter than index_topk -- a prefill property. At decode
+# every sequence is longer than topk, no block is ever all-padding, the guard never fires,
+# and it costs a measured 8% (34.55 -> 37.32 us at bs=64, ctx=9216, topk=2048). The two
+# regimes sit far apart in token count -- decode batches are captured at CUDA-graph sizes
+# (<= 512 here), prefill chunks are --chunked-prefill-size (16384 here) -- so 1024 falls in
+# an empty gap and the split is not sensitive to its exact value. Purely a performance
+# switch: both variants compute the same thing, so a misdispatch costs speed, not answers.
+_SKIP_EMPTY_MIN_TOKENS = 1024
+
+
